course: dictionary
lesson: 8600
title: One word, several meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: One word can have more than one meaning, and the context tells you which one is meant. The word scotch is a good example. «Think of a Scotch egg cut in half at a picnic» is about food, so here a Scotch egg is a boiled egg wrapped in sausage meat and breadcrumbs.
explain: Scotch can also be a verb. In the news, people «scotch rumours», which means they stop a rumour by showing it is false. Test your meaning in the sentence: "they stop the rumour by showing it is false" still makes sense, so you have the right meaning.
explain: With a capital letter, Scotch often appears in fixed names, such as Scotch egg, Scotch tape, Scotch whisky and Scotch mist. Be careful with people: for people from Scotland, say "Scottish" or "Scots", not "Scotch", which many Scottish people find old-fashioned or wrong.
fact: Scotch can be a noun, an adjective or a verb, so check the context.
fact: «Scotch egg» means a boiled egg wrapped in sausage meat and breadcrumbs.
fact: «Scotch» as a verb means to stop a rumour, idea or plan, often by showing it is false.
fact: «Scotch tape» is a US brand of clear sticky tape; in the UK it is called Sellotape.
fact: For people from Scotland, say "Scottish" or "Scots", not "Scotch".
exercise: «Think of a Scotch egg cut in half at a picnic.» What is a Scotch egg? | *A boiled egg wrapped in sausage meat and breadcrumbs | A sweet cake filled with jam | A raw egg in a glass of milk | A fried egg on toast
exercise: The news says the council will «scotch the rumour» about the school closing. What does scotch mean here? | To write the rumour down | To ask a question about the rumour | *To stop the rumour by showing it is false | To spread the rumour far and wide
exercise: «Scotch tape» is a brand name. What is Scotch tape? | Paper for wrapping presents | *Clear sticky tape, a brand from the US | A thick rope from Scotland | A kind of hat
test: Which drink is Scotch whisky? | A fizzy lemon drink | *A drink made in Scotland | A drink made in Italy | A hot milky drink
test: Someone from Scotland asks you to describe them. Which word is the better choice? | Scotch | *Scottish | Scotchman | Scotchy
exam: In «they will scotch the rumour», which part of speech is scotch? | Name | *Verb | Noun | Adjective
